  "dct_description_sm": [
    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us7000rrbj](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us7000rrbj) Magnitude 6.2 earthquake at 52.24 depth occurred on Jan 22 2026 128 km S of Vilyuchinsk, Russia. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude 51.7794 longitude 158.5523. It impacted 83 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
